Laia Abril's "Luto" combines a performance, a single-channel video (9 min 39 sec), and a photographic triptych (pigment inkjet prints on Hahnemühle paper, 230 × 389 cm overall) at the Conservatorio di Musica Benedetto Marcello in Venice.

I provided on-site technical support for the piece which involved creating a system so her videos can be played at proper resolution on the Sony TV from the 80s to create the effect she wanted.

Shown as part of "Lorca en Cataluña: Yo no he nacido todavía," curated by Francisco Ortuño Millán for Art Hub Collective, Venice 2026, May 2026.

[Art Hub Collective](https://www.arthubcollective.art/lorca) · [Laia Abril](https://www.laiaabril.com/exhibition/luto-conservatorio-di-musica-benedetto-marcello-venezia-2026/)
